<%-- Help text of the advanced search form (jsp:include of search/advancedSearch-body.jsp): pulldowns for exact
     searches, entries separated by commas, phrases, lists of codes and "Not equals" (the search rules decided
     2026-10-27, GenericSearch). Docs: docs/flows/search.md. Tests:
     tests/unit/test_decided_pages.py::test_search_help_text_says_phrase_and_exact. --%><p>For a faster search, use the pulldown menus to perform exact searches. Each text box can take several entries, separated by commas; a specimen is found if it matches any of them (with "Not equals": none of them). An entry of several words is searched as one phrase: "Santa Cruz" finds Santa Cruz, not every Santa and every Cruz. Specimen, locality and collection codes may also be separated by spaces or line breaks. "Equals" means the whole entry: in the taxon name box, rufa finds the species (and subspecies) named rufa, not pseudorufa, and "Formica rufa" finds that species.</p>
